after.text:
Surviving a well-read warning is success, not 'too easy' (Creative). So the targets are:
- median 1–2 of your 3 hit points spent per bout (0 = open throws are free: strengthen his normal volley);
- median hits landed by a first-timer (QA): if good players stall around 6–7 of 10, the clock decides the bout. Fix special frequency first; changing the 10 is the host's call;
- abandoned throws (cancelled when the swirl starts): the 'did they interrupt a tempting throw' evidence (Systems).
Also log distance to the nearest mound at swirl start and survived or not. Never shorten the 2.5s warning or the 60s clock.

